From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vincenzopio <43883474+vincenzopio@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:06:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] service: serve only the launcher, on a channel it passes as
 standard input.

The keychain trusts the service's signature, and the service took its keychain namespace from
the environment: any process of the user could run a signed service and ask it for an account's
tokens. A signed service now needs XODUS_LAUNCHER_CHANNEL=stdin and a socket as standard input.
Before it touches the keychain, it checks the socket's peer by its audit token (LOCAL_PEERTOKEN)
against `identifier "dev.macrock.launcher" and certificate leaf = H"..."`, where the leaf is the
service's own certificate: only the holder of that certificate's key can sign such a launcher.
Otherwise it exits with status 78 (EX_CONFIG). A service signed ad hoc, which the keychain trusts
for nothing a release created, may run without the channel, for development and tests.

The channel carries the service's frames with PROTO_MAGIC and the messages of
proto/xodus/launcher.proto. LAUNCHER_HELLO is answered with the channel protocol's version.
Closing the channel stops the service, as a signal does.

Original work for macrock (GPL-3.0-only, as Xodus).

Topic: launcher-channel
